+# Research
+
+## Request paths and current behavior
+
+- Product deletion is handled by `ProductApi.delete` (`sm-shop/.../store/api/v1/product/ProductApi.java`) and `ProductApiV2.deleteV2`, both delegating to `ProductCommonFacadeImpl.deleteProduct`. That method validates the product/store and calls `ProductService.delete`; product deletion removes the catalog entity and related catalog data. There is no order-product relationship that should require deleting order history.
+- The v2 SKU read path (`ProductApiV2` -> `ProductFacadeV2Impl.getProductByCode` -> `ProductService.getBySku`) already throws `ResourceNotFoundException` when no product is found, so a deleted SKU should be 404 once missing-product failures are not accidentally converted elsewhere.
+- Cart add/update paths in `sm-shop/.../store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java` resolve the requested SKU before creating an item. The persisted-cart add path throws `ResourceNotFoundException` when the SKU is absent, which is the required 404 behavior. Multi/update operations first load the existing cart and then use the same item creation path.
+
+## Root causes
+
+- `ShoppingCartServiceImpl.getPopulatedItem` rehydrates a cart item by SKU. `ProductServiceImpl.getBySku` throws `ServiceException` for a missing SKU; the service currently catches that at the outer level, so GET cart fails instead of treating the item as deleted. When it does receive `null`, it marks the item obsolete.
+- `ShoppingCartServiceImpl.getPopulatedShoppingCart` sets a cart-level obsolete flag when any item is obsolete. `getByCode`, `getById`, and `getShoppingCart` then delete/return `null` for the whole cart. This violates the requirement to retain the cart and discard only deleted-product lines, including the single-item case.
+- `ReadableShoppingCartMapper.merge` assumes every line has a non-null live `item.getProduct()` and uses it for product mapping, variants, and attributes. Any stale line that survives hydration would therefore still fail conversion. Cart calculation in `OrderServiceImpl.caculateShoppingCart` also calls `p.getProduct().isAvailable()`, so deleted lines must be removed before calculation.
+- Cart subtotal/total/quantity are recalculated by `ShoppingCartCalculationService` and the cart mapper from the hydrated line items. Once stale lines are removed, empty carts can be calculated as zero and remain addressable for PUT/multi/checkout.
+- `ReadableOrderProductMapper` and the deprecated `ReadableOrderProductPopulator` first copy the denormalized order-product fields (SKU, product name, ordered quantity, one-time charge and calculated subtotal), then optionally enrich the response with the current catalog product. `ProductService.getBySku` throws for a missing SKU, so the readers previously failed before reaching their `product != null` guard; both need to treat that exception as absent optional enrichment. The persisted order fields and `OrderTotal` records remain available after deletion. The order facade uses `ReadableOrderProductMapper` for order reads.
+- Checkout/order creation uses cart line items and `OrderProductPopulator`; stale cart lines must not reach that code. The existing cart hydration cleanup is the appropriate boundary because it affects GET, PUT, multi, and checkout consistently.
+
+## Files likely affected
+
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartServiceImpl.java`: tolerate missing SKU lookups, remove only stale cart items (and their attributes), persist the remaining set, and never mark a non-empty cart obsolete merely because a product was deleted.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/order/OrderServiceImpl.java`: verify calculation is safe for an empty cart after cleanup; likely no behavioral change needed if cleanup guarantees no null products.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/cart/ReadableShoppingCartMapper.java` and possibly the legacy `ShoppingCartDataPopulator`: ensure empty carts serialize with an empty product collection and zero totals, and do not dereference deleted products.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java`: preserve the existing 404 add behavior and verify cart mutation paths continue to use the cleaned cart.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/order/ReadableOrderProductMapper.java`: preserve order snapshot fields while treating live-product enrichment as optional (and test both single and list order reads).
+- Existing integration tests under `sm-shop/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/shop/integration/{cart,order,product}` are the natural test locations; core shopping-cart tests can cover service cleanup without a full HTTP scenario.
+
+## Scope and compatibility notes
+
+- Product deletion must not cascade into `ORDER_PRODUCT`; those rows are the historical snapshot and must remain untouched.
+- Other products should continue to hydrate, recalculate, and serialize normally.
+- Empty carts must remain persisted rather than deleted, because their code is needed for subsequent PUT/multi operations and checkout.
